    Addendum 2 (massless medium): w = 1/3 (radiation-like) gives c_s,eff^2 = c**2/4 > 0 -> no attraction outside the sink; w = -1 has no velocity (1d)
  [PASS] 1e attraction outside the sink with |v| ~ r^-n, 0 < n < 2 (force slower than r^-5) requires c_s^2 = -n v^2/(2 - n) < 0; the deep-MOND log flow requires c_s^2 = -V^2/(2 - 1/(2L)) < 0; a Lambda-like EOS gives c_s,eff^2 = w c^2/(1+w) (= -c^2 at w = -1/2): negative, i.e. a gradient instability, and |c_s| ~ c makes the flow incompressible at galactic speeds (v ~ r^-2, force ~ r^-5); the massless radiation-like w = 1/3 gives +c^2/4: no attraction at all
